    <detaileddescription>
<para>Abstract interfaces for index operations.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="version"><para>0.0.47 </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Maturity: 🟢 PRODUCTION-READY </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Score: 86/100 </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Status: Production Ready </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>This block is auto-generated and will be overwritten.</para>
</simplesect>
This file defines contracts for various index types in ThemisDB:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Secondary indexes (B-tree, hash)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Vector indexes (HNSW, IVF)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Graph indexes (adjacency lists)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Full-text indexes</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Design Goals:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Break circular dependencies between Index ↔ Query ↔ Storage</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Enable isolated unit testing with mock implementations</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Support multiple index implementation strategies</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Allow query engine to use indexes without knowing implementation details</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>This is a Phase 1 interface definition. Implementations will be refactored in subsequent phases to use this interface. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
